  "diagnosis": "two independent failures. CONDITION 1: the newly-explicit per-side materiality check catches the pitcher BENCH bucket (brier 0.07019 -> 0.0703, log-loss 0.25642 -> 0.25999, +1.4% relative vs the 1% tolerance): the pit maps pull mid-grade pitchers' probability mass toward bust at bench's expense, which the pooled view (hitters' large bench gain) masked in E-ISO2. CONDITION 3: within-year cross-side Spearman is unstable under the recalibration; 2020 and 2022 improve (+0.0123, +0.0060) but 2021 (-0.0264) and 2023 (-0.0252) blow through the -0.002 bar by an order of magnitude. This is NOT the E-ISO2 metric-floor artifact: in 2021 the IDENTITY transform scores +0.0141 ABOVE the shipped-grade baseline within-year, so the recalibration itself degrades cross-side interleaving there by ~0.04 rho. Mechanism as diagnosed in E-ISO2: the pit maps compress the top end toward ~FV 44-45, dropping top pitchers below top hitters, and whether that helps or hurts depends on which side's elite cohort hit in a given year, hence the sign flips. The calibration gain itself remains real and large (conditions 2 and 4 pass cleanly: 8/8 within-cell rank preservation; every FV45+ tier improves, tier-45 gap 0.0946 -> 0.0156, tier-55 0.1616 -> 0.0436; FV-35 worse by only 0.00087 vs the 0.005 tolerance).",
  "reading": "the redesigned gate did exactly what it was built to do: it removed the two E-ISO2 objections that production never exercises (cross-year map drift, 1e-4 tier noise) and the method STILL fails on two effects a reader of the board would actually see: a genuinely worse pitcher bench-probability and year-dependent cross-side rank churn. This is a clean rejection of the recalibration, not of the gate.",
  "disposition": "NO SHIP. Per the pre-registration, this is the FINAL loss ledger: no further calibration attempts against this data vintage. Harness (tools/efv_grade_recal3_lab.py) + this artifact are the committed loss."
